## SLOW IT DOWN

Congratulations you are now well and truly drumming, dancing, or both! It's at this point that we check in how you are traveling. Have you had a chance to check out the online videos? Do you find them useful? Is there anything else that would help you on your drumming and/or dancing journey? Do you forget to breathe when you are drumming? Do you forget to smile when you are dancing? Remember, you are drumming and dancing because it is fun! If you are not smiling and breathing, then you are not having fun! ...it will all come together shortly. Below are a few things that we consider important at this point. Feel free to touch base with us on Tuesday if you have questions or concerns.

**Slow It Down**

Are you getting stuck and just can’t seem to get your head around something in particular? Use a slower speed setting on YouTube when you are going over course content. You can learn how to do this [here](https://support.google.com/youtube/answer/7509567?hl=en&co=GENIE.Platform%3DDesktop). Chat with Bec if you have any trouble setting this up.

**Drum & Dance Go Together**

Dancers, we believe that drumming helps your understanding and feeling of the rhythms. So, to help your dance journey **we are offering you one free drum class**. This class has to be drumming and needs to be taken during your first 4-week course. This class is not refundable and cannot be exchanged for a dance class.  This will deepen your understanding, strengthen your connection to the music, and therefore assist your dancing in every way! Take this opportunity to get as much as you can out of your first 4 weeks with us.

**Have Yo****u Experienced Our Trial Drum?**

Drummers, if you are new to all of this it's more than likely you haven't experienced a different drum and that's ok! It's not that you are missing out, it's more like it can just get a whole lot better! I don't want to ignite any FOMO (Fear Of Missing Out), I would just like to bring to your attention a potential for MOMO (Mystery Of Missing Out). This refers to fearing that you are missing out, but have no idea what it is you are missing out on. We want to fill that gap by giving you the chance to play an African drum, professionally made by Nathaniel. You will feel the difference and most importantly hear the difference! You will be surprised at how quickly your playing improves. We only have one of these drums, so book your spot for the next class to experience something different. This could be a game changer or a ROMO (Reality Of Missing Out) which refers to knowing that you are not missing out on anything! You have got nothing to lose!
